# GPU and accelerators

Use Mojo GPU APIs first. Do not emit CUDA C++, HIP, or Triton as the default GPU implementation.

```text
algorithm semantics
    -> generic Mojo kernel/layout
        -> NVIDIA specialization only if measured/required
        -> AMD specialization only if measured/required
```

Keep algorithm, tensor/layout, and scheduling separate from vendor code.

Reason about grid/block/thread mapping, warps/wavefronts, global/shared/local memory, coalescing, registers, sync, occupancy, tiling, vectorization, transfers, and arithmetic intensity.

CPU numerical work: consider `SIMD` before external native libraries.

For matmul, attention, softmax, norms, reductions, embeddings, search, quantization: check Modular/MAX kernels first, reuse when suitable, otherwise implement in Mojo, then test, then benchmark.
